# Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We are committed to providing a welcoming, respectful, and inclusive environment for everyone participating in this project.

We pledge to act and interact in ways that contribute to an open, friendly, and professional community.

## Our Standards

Examples of behavior that contribute to a positive environment include:

- Being respectful and considerate.
- Using welcoming and inclusive language.
- Accepting constructive criticism.
- Focusing on what is best for the community.
- Showing empathy toward other community members.

Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, discrimination, personal attacks, intimidation, and other inappropriate conduct.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing the standards of acceptable behavior.

They may take appropriate and fair corrective action in response to unacceptable behavior.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies within all project spaces and when an individual is officially representing the project or community.

## Enforcement

Instances of unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project maintainers.

All reports will be reviewed and investigated fairly and appropriately.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Project maintainers will consider the circumstances and severity of an incident when determining an appropriate response.

Responses may include a warning, temporary restriction, or permanent removal from project spaces when necessary.

## Attribution

This Code of Conduct is inspired by community standards and open-source Code of Conduct practices.